  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EXPANDING COMPREHENSIVE ADVOCACY TO INFLUENCE LOCAL HUMAN RIGHTS CHANGE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Expanding comprehensive advocacy to influence local human rights change project aims to uphold human rights by supporting and protecting civil society space in 57 target countries in Africa, Asia, the Americas and Eastern Europe. Specifically, it seeks to enable local civil society to mobilise international levers of influence in favour of human rights by; strengthening online and physical coordination between human rights  NGOs and human rights defenders, with a particular focus on women&apos;s human rights NGOs/defenders; increasing  policy influence towards the UN, EU and others; to increase reach to New York and Washington based institutions; and improving  documentation and information on human rights situations and increasing effective public visibility of same.</narrative>
  </description>
